# Mercury 2.5 — findings by Glyph Cluster

- Source: Inception (`inception/mercury-2.5`)
- Date: 2026-11-11 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** Mercury 2.5
- **Short description:** Inception's diffusion large language model (dLLM) positioned as a faster, higher-quality successor to Mercury 2 for latency-sensitive production workloads such as search, voice, and coding support loops. Closed-weights commercial model.
- **Provider / access:** Inception API, Baseten, and OpenRouter; API model id `mercury-2.5` (OpenAI-compatible chat completions per Inception docs). Inception notes launch availability and that Mercury 2.5 was later closed to new users (2026-10-19) in favor of Mercury 3 (per local meta context).
- **Release / knowledge:** Announced by Inception in 2026 (blog: "Introducing Mercury 2.5"); knowledge cutoff not stated in verified public sources found.
- **IDs:** `inception/mercury-2.5` (no Free ID on Zen; `noFreeId` per local meta).
- **Context window:** 260,000 tokens total; 65,536 max output tokens (per Inception models documentation).
- **Modalities:** Text in, text out; reasoning controls, parallel tool calls, and schema-aligned JSON supported (per Inception announcement/docs).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-11-11):** $0.20 / $0.75 per 1M input/output tokens, $0.02 cached input (Inception list). Launch promotion reported at $0.04 / $0.15 per 1M input/output; OpenRouter/Vercel listings referenced in local meta reflect launch pricing. Closed to new users after 2026-10-19 per local meta.
- **Architecture:** Proprietary diffusion LLM; parameter count not publicly disclosed.

